{
  "_about": "How Shopify order lines become retention products. Shopify's own product type decides what is not a product: Freebie, Merch, Book and Gummies lines never count, and neither do zero-value or free-gift lines. Every other paid line is a named product; sets and gift boxes that are no longer on the website are grouped so nothing is lost. Titles are lower-cased, non-ASCII characters become spaces and runs of spaces collapse before any pattern is tried. Patterns use only the regex features Python and BigQuery (RE2) share, so the same rules can be run in SQL to check coverage. Order matters: the first matching rule wins.",
  "exclude_always": [
    {
      "reason": "free gift or test line",
      "pattern": "\\bfree\\b|^_|^test|pay remaining amount"
    }
  ],
  "exclude_unless_product": [
    {
      "reason": "merch",
      "pattern": "\\bcharm\\b|\\btote\\b|\\bbag\\b|\\bpouch\\b|tumbler|sticker|sipper|\\bmug\\b"
    }
  ],
